{
  "_": [
    "v0.47.0 D1 — the task-line grammar, pinned as shared vectors.",
    "",
    "Each case is one markdown block and the tasks it holds, in document order. Consumed by",
    "packages/core/src/markdown/tasks.rs today; the TS consumers (the editor's live preview, Docli",
    "Connect) take the same file when they start reading tasks, so the grammar has ONE written",
    "contract across release trains.",
    "",
    "`line` is 1-based in the note body. `parent` is the ordinal of the nearest enclosing CHECKBOX (a task or, since v0.47.1, a checklist item) (a",
    "plain bullet in between is skipped). A provisional identity's `hash` is FNV-1a 32-bit over the",
    "line from the list bullet to its end (trailing whitespace trimmed), as 8 lowercase hex digits.",
    "`%%…%%` comment text is removed before the line is read.",
    "",
    "v0.47.1 — `isTask`: a checkbox is a TASK when it carries a signal (a `^t-` id, a reserved field,",
    "a date emoji, or a `[/]` `[h]` `[-]` state); a bare one is a checklist item. A note's frontmatter",
    "boolean `tasks` overrides (`true` every checkbox, `false` none); `switch` is that value when a",
    "case sets it (absent = no boolean switch).",
    "",
    "v0.47.5 — `tags`: the `#tags` the note's tag pass finds on the task's OWN line, after its marker",
    "(not a child line's, not the note's; code excluded), one per tag ignoring case with the first",
    "spelling kept. Absent when the line has none."
  ],
